{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to understand the structure of Pascal's Triangle and the arithmetic mean of its elements in the \\(n\\)th row. The \\(n\\)th row of Pascal's Triangle is given by the binomial coefficients \\(\\binom{n}{0}, \\binom{n}{1}, \\ldots, \\binom{n}{n}\\).\n\nThe sum of the elements in the \\(n\\)th row of Pascal's Triangle is \\(2^n\\). This is a well-known property of binomial coefficients. Therefore, the arithmetic mean of the elements in the \\(n\\)th row is given by the total sum of the elements divided by the number of elements, which is \\(2^n / (n+1)\\).\n\n","prefix_end":571,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,3535,279,5944,315,57359,594,38031,323,279,34784,3076,315,1181,5424,304,279,17767,77,57758,339,2802,13,576,17767,77,57758,339,2802,315,57359,594,38031,374,2661,553,279,9544,20855,36829,1124,11520,6863,316,91362,15170,15,2137,1124,6863,316,91362,15170,16,2137,1124,507,2412,11,1124,6863,316,91362,15170,77,11035,3593,785,2629,315,279,5424,304,279,17767,77,57758,339,2802,315,57359,594,38031,374,17767,17,86167,59,568,1096,374,264,1632,21309,3343,315,9544,20855,36829,13,15277,11,279,34784,3076,315,279,5424,304,279,17767,77,57758,339,2802,374,2661,553,279,2790,2629,315,279,5424,17779,553,279,1372,315,5424,11,892,374,17767,17,86167,608,320,77,10,16,10699,3593,1654,525,2661,429,279,34784,3076,315,279,5424,304,279,17767,77,57758,339,2802,374,220,20,16,13,17,13,2055,11,582,646,3270,279,23606,510,59,9640,59,37018,90,17,86167,15170,77,10,16,92,284,220,20,16,13,17,198,59,921,1249,1477,17767,77,59,701,582,1184,311,11625,419,23606,13,5512,11,582,646,18130,220,20,16,13,17,438,264,19419,510,59,9640,20,16,13,17,284,1124,37018,90,20,16,17,15170,16,15,92,284,1124,37018,90,17,20,21,15170,20,532,59,921,44500,11,279,23606,9044,510,59,9640,59,37018,90,17,86167,15170,77